.TH AINIX 1 "October 2026" "AINIX 0.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ainix \- local NixOS assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ainix
[\,OPTIONS\/] [\,QUERY\/]
.SH DESCRIPTION
AINIX is a local assistant for NixOS. It answers from a small knowledge
base, real Nix tools, optional web search, and an optional local model.
.PP
Default help order is docs-first. Model-first is optional.
Preview is the default for control. Nothing runs unless you pass
\fB--execute\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B help
Show usage.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.B \-\-history
Recent queries.
.TP
.B \-\-note TEXT
Save a note.
.TP
.B \-\-cache-clear
Clear doc cache.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove the curl-installed files.
.TP
.B \-\-model NAME
Ollama model to use (optional).
.TP
.B \-\-model-first
Ask the local model first.
.TP
.B \-\-docs-first
Docs and web first (default).
.TP
.B \-\-execute, \-x
Run a control command (asks unless \fB--yes\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-yes, \-y
Skip confirm on execute.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ainix/config.json
Optional: {"model": "gemma2:9b", "model_first": true}
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ainix/
History, notes, cache.
.SH NOTES
Model is optional and hardware-agnostic. No NVIDIA/AMD assumptions.
AINIX does not edit your config files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nix (1),
.BR nixos-rebuild (8)
